# vehje-runtime-abi. backlog

Designed but deferred. Names stay unbackticked until they ship.

## The extern "C" export with the panic-handler story

The batched-column entry's type surface and layout are now-work; the actual
`extern "C"` export lands with the panic-free C-host embedding story (a panic
must not cross the boundary; error codes and the Outcome-shaped return carry
failure). The signature is defined now, the export with its panic guard lands
with the driver bindings.

## The stencil section producer

The residual and package wire carry a reserved stencil section from day one; its
producer is the deferred copy-and-patch stencil toolchain. The slot exists, the
bytes come later.

## The per-reference generational flag

The wire carries a schema slot for the per-reference generational-reference flag
the mutable-consumer lease residual sets at the avoidance boundary; its semantics
are set by the Zig-side check. Schema-now, semantics-later.

## The three bench-gated format decisions

The node record inline-operand count, the region-id column width (a flags byte
when the live-region count is small, else a parallel array), and whether the
native tier beats the cheap-lowered interpreter enough to justify the stencil
trusted base are measure-then-lock constants with provisional values, to lock
against a census-specific corpus when real consumers exist.

## The bytecode tier encoder

The `Tier` bytecode form's encoder is deferred; the arena form is the reference
semantics and ships first.
